  "id": "pluralism",
  "term": "pluralism",
  "definition": "In this context, pluralism means the coexistence of multiple psychotherapy approaches that describe similar clinical processes using different, non-matching languages or models. It can be clinically useful because it preserves meaningful distinctions across schools, but it also makes comparison and shared representation harder.",
